# Custom merge driver for DERIVED / APPEND-ONLY registry JSON files that every migration PR touches.
# Without this, any migration PR that merges first conflicts EVERY other open migration PR on these
# single shared files, and hand-resolving them then fails `verify:schema-parity` in CI. The json-union
# driver (scripts/git-merge-driver.mjs, registered by scripts/setup-git-merge-drivers.mjs) deep-unions
# both sides automatically so `git merge origin/main` never surfaces a conflict on them. The post-merge
# hook then canonicalizes the schema-parity baseline via `--update` (pure static, no DB).
docs/schema-parity-baseline.json        merge=json-union
db/migrations/.held-migrations.json     merge=json-union
scripts/verify-steps/CLAIMED-NUMBERS.json      merge=json-union
scripts/entity-isolation-allowlist.json merge=json-union

# MODULE-COMPLETION MANIFEST TREADMILL KILLER (2026-07-29): every Cursor money PR edits
# docs/module-completion/{accounting,banking,lists}.json (evidence / status). Plain 3-way merge
# conflicts every parallel PR; array-by-value union would DUPLICATE same-id items. Driver uses
# keyed union on items[].id / ranked_findings[].id (see scripts/git-merge-driver.mjs).
docs/module-completion/*.json           merge=json-union

# CONFLICT-TREADMILL KILLER (2026-07-13): every guard/verify PR appends a `verify:*` script to
# package.json and a run-step to locked-guards.yml at the SAME tail anchor, so whichever PR merges
# first conflicts EVERY other open PR on these two files — the endless hand-resolve treadmill.
#   - package.json: the json-union driver deep-unions the scripts object (verified: JSON.parse →
#     JSON.stringify(_,null,2) roundtrips package.json byte-identically, so unchanged content never
#     churns — only the newly-added keys from both sides survive). Driver auto-registered by the
#     `prepare` npm script (scripts/setup-git-merge-drivers.mjs) on every install.
#   - locked-guards.yml: git's built-in `union` driver keeps BOTH sides of an append-only conflict
#     hunk (the guard step list only ever grows at the tail), yielding valid YAML with every branch's
#     steps. (union is line-based — safe here BECAUSE we only ever APPEND guard steps, never edit
#     existing lines; keep it that way.)
package.json                            merge=json-union
.github/workflows/locked-guards.yml     merge=union

# PARITYTABLE TRACKER TREADMILL KILLER (2026-07-20): every ParityTable migration PR appends a section
# to this one shared tracker, so whichever PR merged first conflicted EVERY other open ParityTable PR
# on it — PRs then went stale, were closed, and were re-opened as fresh duplicates (#2882/#2891,
# #2892/#2874, #2893/#2896 …), which is what produced the duplicate-PR churn.
#   PRECONDITION (do not skip): `union` is LINE-BASED and is only correct on an APPEND-ONLY file. This
#   file qualifies ONLY because its Rollup counts were converted to DERIVED in the same commit that
#   added this rule. Before that change the rollup was edited in place by every PR, and union-merging
#   it would have kept BOTH sides of each count line — silently duplicating rows rather than
#   conflicting. That corruption had already accumulated by hand-resolve: 12 rollup rows instead of 4,
#   with three contradictory `pending` values. If anyone re-introduces an edited-in-place count or
#   any other mutable line here, REMOVE this union rule in the same PR or the corruption returns
#   silently — a duplicated row is not a merge failure, so CI will not catch it.
docs/trackers/PARITYTABLE-MIGRATION-TRACKER.md  merge=union

# LST-PICKER / VERIFY-STEP CLAIM TREADMILL KILLER (2026-07-30):
# Every LST-PICKER slice (and every new verify-step) touches CLAIMED-NUMBERS.json. Without a union
# driver, whichever PR merges first conflicts EVERY sibling on that registry — hours of hand rebase
# with zero product progress (same class as package.json / held-migrations before their drivers).
# json-union deep-merges the `claimed` object so both sides' numbers survive.
scripts/verify-steps/CLAIMED-NUMBERS.json       merge=json-union

# Same treadmill on catalogPickerRegistry.ts: each picker slice ADDS one top-level config key.
# catalog-picker-union keep-alls keys from both sides (theirs wins on same-key collision).
apps/frontend/src/components/parity/catalogPickerRegistry.ts  merge=catalog-picker-union

# PARTIAL LST-PICKER evidence notes are APPEND-ONLY — never edit lists.json evidence for PARTIAL
# slices (that file's evidence string is one in-place line → guaranteed conflict). Append here.
docs/module-completion/lists-picker-partials.md merge=union

# PHANTOM-COLUMN ALLOWLIST (2026-07-31): every phantom-column fix retires a key from this ratchet, so
# two parallel fixes always both edit it — the same magnet-file shape as CLAIMED-NUMBERS.json. Without
# a union driver they conflict on merge; with one they merge cleanly AND (via the .gitattributes-derived
# exemption in branch-precheck-push.mjs / verify-branch-fresh.mjs) stop forcing rebases.
scripts/verify-sql-column-existence.allowlist.json      merge=json-union
